{%- comment -%}
================================================================================
  LUCKY GOLF · BUY 2 GET 1 FREE — HATS
  Shopify section. Drop-in, self-contained, theme-agnostic.

  THREE RULES THIS FILE FOLLOWS, EACH LEARNED THE HARD WAY:

  1. THE DISCOUNT OWNS THE MONEY, NOT THIS PAGE.
     A storefront cannot set a line price to zero. All three hats are added at
     full price and Shopify's automatic "Buy 2 get 1 free" discount zeroes one
     at checkout. Every figure the reader sees is read back out of /cart.js
     (final_line_price, original_line_price), so if the discount is off, or
     capped, or changed, the page tells the truth instead of its own guess.

  2. NOTHING LEAKS INTO THE THEME, AND THE THEME CANNOT LEAK IN.
     Every class is prefixed lgb-/bgo- and every custom property is declared on
     .lg-bogo, not :root. An earlier build of this page reused a bare class
     name that already meant something else in the host stylesheet and every
     product drew a second frame inside its own card. Assume every generic
     name is taken.

  3. THE CATALOGUE IS READ, NEVER RETYPED.
     Hats come from the chosen collection; upsell options and variants come
     from the products themselves. Sold-out sizes and dead loft/grind
     combinations disable themselves because Shopify says so, not because
     somebody remembered to update a list.
================================================================================
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign hat_col = section.settings.hats_collection -%}
{%- assign bundle_size = section.settings.bundle_size | default: 3 -%}

<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:ital,wdth,wght@0,62..125,100..900;1,62..125,100..900&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

{%- comment -%}
  Liquid has no array push, so the four upsell slots are flattened into one
  delimited string and re-split. Field separator is ~F~ and record separator ~R~. Do NOT use runs of
  the same character: an empty one-liner made "~|~" + "" + "~~~" collide,
  and the record split landed mid-field. Trailing empty fields are dropped by
  Liquid's split, so bits[2] is simply nil when a one-liner is blank, which a one-liner is free text and will contain commas and pipes.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign up = '' -%}
{%- if section.settings.apparel_1 != blank -%}{%- assign up = up | append: section.settings.apparel_1.handle | append: '~F~apparel~F~' | append: section.settings.why_1 | append: '~R~' -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if section.settings.apparel_2 != blank -%}{%- assign up = up | append: section.settings.apparel_2.handle | append: '~F~apparel~F~' | append: section.settings.why_2 | append: '~R~' -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if section.settings.club_1 != blank -%}{%- assign up = up | append: section.settings.club_1.handle | append: '~F~club~F~' | append: section.settings.why_3 | append: '~R~' -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if section.settings.club_2 != blank -%}{%- assign up = up | append: section.settings.club_2.handle | append: '~F~club~F~' | append: section.settings.why_4 | append: '~R~' -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign up_rows = up | split: '~R~' -%}

<script type="application/json" id="lgb-data">
{
  "bundle": {{ bundle_size | json }},
  "cartUrl": {{ routes.cart_url | json }},
  "hats": [
    {%- assign sep = '' -%}
    {%- for product in hat_col.products -%}
      {%- assign v = product.variants.first -%}
      {%- if v.id -%}
        {{ sep }}{
          "id": {{ v.id | json }},
          "name": {{ product.title | json }},
          "url": {{ product.url | json }},
          "img": {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 600 | default: '' | json }},
          "price": {{ v.price | json }},
          "available": {{ v.available | json }}
        }
        {%- assign sep = ',' -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  ],
  "upsell": [
    {%- assign sep2 = '' -%}
    {%- for rowstr in up_rows -%}
      {%- assign bits = rowstr | split: '~F~' -%}
      {%- assign p = all_products[bits[0]] -%}
      {%- if p.id -%}
        {{ sep2 }}{
          "handle": {{ p.handle | json }},
          "group": {{ bits[1] | json }},
          "name": {{ p.title | json }},
          "url": {{ p.url | json }},
          "img": {{ p.featured_image | image_url: width: 400 | default: '' | json }},
          "price": {{ p.price_min | json }},
          "why": {{ bits[2] | default: '' | strip | json }},
          "options": [
            {%- for o in p.options_with_values -%}
              { "name": {{ o.name | json }}, "values": [{%- for val in o.values -%}{{ val.name | default: val | json }}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}{%- endfor -%}] }{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          ],
          "variants": [
            {%- for v in p.variants -%}
              { "id": {{ v.id | json }}, "opts": {{ v.options | json }},
                "available": {{ v.available | json }}, "price": {{ v.price | json }} }{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          ]
        }
        {%- assign sep2 = ',' -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  ]
}
</script>

<div class="lg-bogo" id="lg-bogo">

